 "notes": "Own row has no pool, pit or grave. SWP Rujm el Mogheifir (linked in Stage 1b) coded position none as the unit; WBADB gives that name to S2629 (200 m S) and Nigro to N78/N79 (4-20 m), so its point is uncertain. Birket Jiljulieh (SWP) and the Arab graveyard north of it placed at S2531, whose other names include Birket Jiljulieh and Shejeret el-Ithleh. S2531 pool coded from its other names only. SWP Kanat Musa (Mem III p. 202) describes aqueducts and cisterns at other places (Mefjir, Bir Heider, Birket Musa), none within 2 km per the packet: ignored. Nigro dated L where the reservoir is listed only under Byzantine."
